or": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FdQTyEqdyrycZ7aQQbqyU9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53313, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FdQTyEqdyrycZ7aQQbqyU9", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54712, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019zmdegqdMeabATi6vfQ9MU", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55012, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019zmdegqdMeabATi6vfQ9MU", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55012, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019zmdegqdMeabATi6vfQ9MU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59337, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what happened.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release history shows v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were unhealthy.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions.\n  - I tried once more, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat. That attempt finished, and us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0.\n- **Health:** The service now passes health checks. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created, so I didn't send it a second time, and the on-call engineer was paged once. It covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - finding why v2.3.1 failed\n  - looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012AdcUjbgQ9aEBqsuuKbicr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WQBPp7Wn4awJm7JCSBv9zG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SygUZqFYVZuSafJ4JGpZ6G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HEajnQqPLT4qpwYWnhAuCD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016sZCvzEnrd3YagqFBkik6d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KjFR3YnX4bDa1TGBLkescd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AFVGFfhCymsqTaLHTzyvmr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FdQTyEqdyrycZ7aQQbqyU9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019zmdegqdMeabATi6vfQ9MU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what happened.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release history shows v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were unhealthy.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions.\n  - I tried once more, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat. That attempt finished, and us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0.\n- **Health:** The service now passes health checks. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created, so I didn't send it a second time, and the on-call engineer was paged once. It covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - finding why v2.3.1 failed\n  - looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback", "type": "text"}]}]}